# OrderAudit – Conceptual ER Diagram

> Simplified conceptual view based on the inspected table groups. Confirm all foreign keys against the final SQL schema.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    CUSTOMERS ||--o{ SALES_ORDER_HEADERS : places
    SALES_ORDER_HEADERS ||--|{ SALES_ORDER_ITEMS : contains
    CUSTOMERS ||--o{ INVOICE_HEADERS : receives
    INVOICE_HEADERS ||--|{ INVOICE_ITEMS : contains
    INVOICE_HEADERS ||--o{ CUSTOMER_PAYMENTS : receives
    SUPPLIERS ||--o{ PURCHASE_HEADERS : supplies
    PURCHASE_HEADERS ||--|{ PURCHASE_ITEMS : contains
    PRODUCTS ||--o{ BOM_HEADERS : has
    BOM_HEADERS ||--|{ BOM_ITEMS : defines
    RAW_MATERIALS ||--o{ BOM_ITEMS : required_in
    BOM_HEADERS ||--o{ PRODUCTION_RUNS : used_for
    PRODUCTION_RUNS ||--o{ PRODUCTION_CONSUMPTION : records
    RAW_MATERIALS ||--o{ PRODUCTION_CONSUMPTION : consumed
    PRODUCTION_RUNS ||--o{ PRODUCTION_OUTPUTS : produces
    PRODUCTS ||--o{ PRODUCTION_OUTPUTS : output_product
```

Stock movements are a separate ledger of inventory changes and source references. Units are referenced by product, material, BOM and transaction quantities.
